# Docker build-context excludes.
#
# Patterns without `**` are root-relative: `node_modules/` alone does NOT match
# `frontend/node_modules/`, which used to ship ~218 MB of developer
# dependencies into the context on every build. Always anchor recursive
# exclusions with `**/`.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/coverage/
**/.e2e/
**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/
*.tsbuildinfo
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.husky/
.github/

# Markdown is documentation, not build input. THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md is the
# exception: the Dockerfile copies it into the images' /licenses/ directory.
*.md
!THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md

.eslintrc*
.prettierrc*
vitest.config.ts
playwright.config.ts

# Compose files describe how to run the image; they are never build input.
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.unbound.yml
docker-compose.prod.yml
.coverage-check/

data/
.env*

# Stray migration rollback locks (see .gitignore).
..locks/
**/..locks/
